{
  "choices": [
    {
      "message": {
        "content": "{\n  \"source_routes\": [\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0181\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"A specific enterotype derived from gut microbiome of older individuals enables favorable responses to immune checkpoint blockade therapy.\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"CH01\",\n        \"CH03\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该研究识别出老年患者特有的“衰老富集肠型”，并通过荟萃分析显示其与更好的ICB反应相关。小鼠FMT实验证实该肠型可重塑肿瘤微环境（增加细胞毒性T细胞），提示年龄作为宿主因素通过特定微生物群落调节ICI疗效。可用于讨论宿主背景（年龄）对微生物 - 免疫轴的特异性影响及机制验证。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0182\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"The Gut Microbiome Associates with Immune Checkpoint Inhibition Outcomes in Patients with Advanced Non–Small Cell Lung Cancer\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"CH01\",\n        \"CH02\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"在日本NSCLC队列中，发现Ruminococcaceae UCG 13和Agathobacter富集与更好预后正相关，而基线抗生素使用显著降低这些菌丰度并削弱疗效关联。该研究提供了特定菌属作为预测标志物的观察性证据，并强调了抗生素作为关键混杂因素在解释微生物组 - 疗效关联中的重要性。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0183\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Microbial Influence on Immune Checkpoint Inhibitor Therapy in Non-Small Cell Carcinoma: The Gut–Lung-Immune Axis\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"CH02\",\n        \"CH03\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该综述详细阐述了“肠 - 肺 - 免疫轴”机制，包括肠道代谢物（SCFAs）系统性调节免疫、抗原激活树突状细胞招募T细胞至肺部，以及肿瘤内微生物直接调节局部微环境。它提供了从肠道到肺部肿瘤的多层次机制框架，并列举了Akkermansia等具体菌属在NSCLC中的临床关联证据。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0184\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"The science of tumor-infiltrating lymphocytes (TIL): perspectives from the SITC Surgery Committee\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"CH03\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"虽主要聚焦TIL疗法，但该综述指出有利的肠道微生物组组成与增强的全身性及抗肿瘤免疫力相关，可能通过调节肿瘤免疫微环境发挥作用。可作为背景材料，说明微生物组在广义癌症免疫治疗（包括细胞疗法）中调节T细胞功能的普遍性原理，补充ICI机制讨论。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0185\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Impact of Concomitant Proton Pump Inhibitor Use on the Efficacy of Immune Checkpoint Inhibitors Across Multiple Cancer Types.\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"CH01\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"大规模观察性研究显示，伴随使用质子泵抑制剂（PPIs）与多种实体瘤患者ICI治疗后死亡率显著增加及ICU入院率升高相关。虽未直接提供微生物机制数据，但该临床现象为“药物 - 微生物相互作用”假说提供了强有力的流行病学动机，提示需关注共用药对微生物介导疗效的潜在干扰。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0186\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Abstract 2861: Comparative genomics of gut commensal Lachnospiraceae and their associations with cancer treatment response with immune checkpoint inhibitors\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"CH02\",\n        \"CH03\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"通过比较毛螺菌科内不同菌株基因组，发现仅特定Blautia物种（而非同科其他菌）能增强ICI疗效。研究基于基因组预测了乙酸生产、叶酸合成等四种潜在分子机制路径。该材料强调了菌株水平特异性效应的重要性，并为代谢物介导的免疫调节提供了具体的生化线索。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0187\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Prognostic Factors for Checkpoint Inhibitor Based Immunotherapy: An Update With New Evidences\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"CH02\",\n        \"CH03\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该综述区分了不同ICI类别（CTLA-4 vs PD-1）相关的有益菌群（如Bacteroides, Bifidobacterium, A. muciniphila），并指出抗生素使用可导致原发耐药。它提出了树突状细胞激活和T细胞募集等机制假设，同时强调了不同癌种和人群中微生物标志物的异质性，为理解疗效差异提供背景。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0188\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Intestinal fungal signatures and their impact on immune checkpoint inhibitor efficacy: a multi-cohort meta-analysis\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"CH02\",\n        \"CH03\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"多队列荟萃分析揭示了肠道真菌（而非仅细菌）与ICI疗效的关联，发现Aspergillus主导型与较好预后相关，而Debaryomyces hansenii通过减少CD8+ T细胞浸润抑制疗效。小鼠实验初步验证了特定真菌的因果作用。该研究拓展了微生物组视角至真菌界，并提供了真菌调节T细胞功能的具体机制线索。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0189\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Reprogramming the tumor microenvironment: synergistic mechanisms of antibody–drug conjugates and immune checkpoint inhibitors\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"CH03\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"虽聚焦ADCs，但该综述详细阐明了诱导免疫原性细胞死亡（ICD）和DAMPs释放如何将“冷”肿瘤转化为“热”肿瘤，为理解ICI起效所需的微环境前提提供了背景。文中提及微生物组调节作为未来方向，可类比说明外部干预如何通过重塑微环境增强ICI敏感性，丰富机制讨论的维度。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0190\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Outer Membrane Vesicles From The Gut Microbiome Contribute to Tumor Immunity by Eliciting Cross-Reactive T Cells\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"CH03\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该研究证明肠道细菌外膜囊泡（OMVs）可通过“分子模拟”机制诱导交叉反应性T细胞，使其从肠道迁移至肿瘤部位并抑制生长。即使无活菌定植，OMVs也能触发此免疫监视机制。这为解释微生物组如何通过抗原特异性途径直接激活抗肿瘤免疫提供了具体的分子载体和实验证据。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0191\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"The Role of Immune Checkpoint Inhibitors in Renal Cancer: Innovation, Resistance Mechanisms, and Next-generation Strategies\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"CH02\",\n        \"CH04\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"针对肾细胞癌，该综述总结了Akkermansia等有益菌与ICI疗效的正相关性，并提及抗生素的负面影响。它概述了微生物组通过代谢产物（SCFAs、色氨酸代谢物）调节全身免疫的机制，并讨论了FMT和益生菌作为克服耐药策略的潜力，为特定癌种的微生物干预提供背景。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0192\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Gut microbiota influence immunotherapy responses: mechanisms and therapeutic strategies\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"CH03\",\n        \"CH04\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该综述系统阐述了微生物群调节ICI疗效的分子机制，包括特定细菌激活DC/CD8+ T细胞、代谢物（肌苷、SCFAs）通过A2AR/HDAC/STING通路 signaling，以及抗原交叉反应。它还比较了FMT、益生菌等干预策略的临床数据，为机制章节提供详细通路图景，并为治疗干预章节提供策略对比。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0193\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Veillonella and Streptococcus are associated with aging of the gut microbiota and affect the efficacy of immune checkpoint inhibitors\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"CH01\",\n        \"CH03\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"在实体瘤患者中，发现Veillonella在年轻/高响应组较高，而Streptococcus在老年/高响应组较高，提示年龄调节微生物标志物的方向。研究提出Streptococcus可能通过诱导CD8+ T细胞浸润增强疗效的假说。该材料可用于讨论宿主因素（年龄）如何改变微生物 - 免疫互作的具体模式及预测价值。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0194\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Microbiome-Driven Diagnostic and Therapeutic Strategies in Cancer\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"CH02\",\n        \"CH03\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该综述列举了Akkermansia等菌属与ICI疗效正相关的临床证据，并指出抗生素使用的负面影响。它从免疫调节（T细胞浸润、抗原呈递）、代谢产物（SCFA）及屏障功能等多角度解释了潜在机制。此外，还涵盖了化疗与微生物组的相互作用，为全面理解微生物组在癌症治疗中的角色提供背景。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0195\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"The microbial metabolite desaminotyrosine enhances T-cell priming and cancer immunotherapy with immune checkpoint inhibitors\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"CH03\",\n        \"CH04\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该研究揭示微生物代谢物DAT通过宿主IFN-I信号通路增强T细胞致敏和DC成熟，从而提升ICI疗效。在抗生素诱导菌群失调的小鼠模型中，外源性补充DAT能部分恢复抗CTLA-4疗效。这为代谢物介导的系统性免疫调节提供了具体的分子路径，并展示了单一代谢物作为潜在补救策略的可行性。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0196\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Emerging Roles of Immunometabolism and Microbiota Crosstalk in Cancer Therapy: A Comprehensive Review\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"CH03\",\n        \"CH05\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该综述引入免疫代谢视角，解释TME内的代谢竞争（如乳酸、葡萄糖缺乏）如何影响免疫细胞对微生物信号的响应。它详细描述了SCFAs、色氨酸代谢物等通过表观遗传和受体信号调节免疫的机制，并讨论了FMT标准化困难等转化挑战。有助于理解为何有益菌群在某些患者中失效及未来研究方向。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0197\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Abstract 2210: Microbiome profiling reveals that fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT) modulates response and toxicity when combined with immunotherapy in patients with lung cancer and melanoma (FMT-LUMINate NCT04951583)\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"CH01\",\n        \"CH04\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"早期临床试验显示FMT联合ICI在NSCLC和黑色素瘤中具有高ORR，但毒性谱系差异巨大（双药联合导致高比例严重irAE）。研究识别出P. copri定植与严重irAE（特别是心肌炎）相关，以及响应者特有的代谢物特征。该材料提供了FMT临床获益/风险平衡的直接数据，并提示特定菌群与毒性的关联。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0198\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"73 Fasting mediated gut microbiome modulation improves response to immune checkpoint therapy in Renal Cell Cancer\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"CH03\",\n        \"CH04\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该研究展示了限时进食通过重塑肠道微生物组和代谢物（如色氨酸代谢物）增强肾癌对ICI的反应。FMT实验证明了微生物组介导效应的因果性。它连接了饮食干预、微生物组改变与临床结局，为“饮食 - 微生物组 - 免疫”轴提供了实证数据，支持非药物干预策略的可行性。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0199\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Baseline gut microbiota composition is associated with oral mucositis and tumour recurrence in patients with head and neck cancer: a pilot study\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"CH02\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"虽针对头颈癌放化疗，但该试点研究发现Faecalibacterium等基线菌属与较低肿瘤复发风险相关，并推测其具有免疫调节功能。可作为微生物组影响实体瘤治疗预后的旁证，提示某些有益菌可能通过通用免疫机制改善治疗结局，尽管需区分治疗模态（放疗vs ICI）的差异。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0200\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Integrative stratification of response to immunotherapy using host and microbial signatures in patients with advanced non-small cell lung cancer\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"CH01\",\n        \"CH02\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该研究开发了基于特定菌群（Faecalibacterium, Lactobacillus等）比率的微生物评分，并在NSCLC队列中验证其预测ICI疗效的价值。纵向数据显示响应者治疗后微生物组向健康状态回归。它提供了动态监测微生物组变化的实证，并展示了微生物特征与TMB结合的互补分层策略。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0201\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"A Natural Polyphenol Exerts Antitumor Activity and Circumvents Anti–PD-1 Resistance through Effects on the Gut Microbiota\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"CH03\",\n        \"CH04\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该研究发现天然多酚castalagin通过特异性富集Ruminococcus/Alistipes，改变胆汁酸代谢并增加CD8+ T细胞浸润，从而逆转小鼠模型中的抗PD-1耐药。FMT实验证实了微生物组的介导作用。这为益生元干预通过特定菌群 - 代谢物轴克服ICI耐药提供了完整的机制链条和实验证据。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0202\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Novel Biomarkers and Druggable Targets in Advanced Melanoma\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"CH02\",\n        \"CH03\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该综述总结了黑色素瘤中肠道微生物组特征（高多样性、特定菌属）与抗PD-1响应的关联，指出抗生素使用削弱疗效。它提出了微生物通过增加CD8+ T细胞浸润增强抗肿瘤免疫的机制假说，并提及微生物组与免疫性结肠炎的潜在联系，为理解疗效与毒性的双重调节提供背景。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0203\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"The impact of the human gut microbiome in the treatment of autoimmune disease\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"CH03\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"虽聚焦自身免疫病，但该综述引用了肿瘤学证据（如FMT来自响应者优于非响应者、A. muciniphila增强疗效），说明微生物组调节免疫治疗疗效的通用机制。它强调了T细胞浸润等宿主免疫机制的重要性，可作为跨疾病比较的背景，提示微生物 - 免疫互作的基本原理可能具有共性。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0204\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Characterizations of multi-kingdom gut microbiota in immune checkpoint inhibitor-treated hepatocellular carcinoma\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"CH02\",\n        \"CH03\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"在HCC患者中，该研究发现细菌和代谢物组成与ICI疗效显著相关，而真菌差异较小。构建了基于18种细菌的预测模型，并识别了与生存相关的特定物种和代谢物。它强调了多界微生物组（细菌 + 真菌 + 代谢物）的复杂视角，为理解不同微生物类群在疗效中的异质性贡献提供实证。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0205\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Correlation of distribution characteristics and dynamic changes of gut microbiota with the efficacy of immunotherapy in EGFR-mutated non-small cell lung cancer\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"CH01\",\n        \"CH02\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"针对EGFR突变NSCLC这一特殊亚群，研究发现抗生素使用显著恶化PFS，而益生菌无效。鉴定出不同于EGFR野生型的特定微生物标志物（如Bradyrhizobium）和代谢物（脱氧胆酸）。该材料揭示了驱动基因突变如何塑造独特的微生物 - 免疫互作模式，提示通用生物标志物可能不适用。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0206\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Microbiome and Cancers, With Focus on Genitourinary Tumors\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"CH02\",\n        \"CH03\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该综述提供了泌尿生殖系统肿瘤中微生物组与ICI疗效关联的证据，特别是抗生素使用预测RCC和UC的耐药性。它详细描述了A. muciniphila产生SCFAs通过GPR受体和HDAC抑制增强T细胞功能的分子模型。可作为特定癌种（RCC/UC）的机制背景和临床关联素材。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0207\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"IUPHAR Review: Targeted Therapies of Signaling Pathways Based on the Gut Microbiome in Autism Spectrum Disorders: Mechanistic and Therapeutic Applications.\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该论文主要关注自闭症谱系障碍（ASD），属于神经发育疾病，其病理生理机制（神经炎症）与实体瘤ICI治疗（T细胞介导的抗肿瘤免疫）存在本质差异。虽然提及微生物代谢物调节免疫，但缺乏肿瘤特异性背景，直接外推风险极高，故不纳入本综述。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0208\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Gut Microbiome Alterations in Colorectal Cancer: Mechanisms, Therapeutic Strategies, and Precision Oncology Perspectives\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"CH02\",\n        \"CH03\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该综述详细描述了结直肠癌中有益菌（Akkermansia, Faecalibacterium）与致病菌对ICI反应的不同影响，并区分了MSI/MSS亚型的微生物特征差异。它阐述了SCFAs在生理与治疗背景下的双重作用，以及微生物通过DC成熟和T细胞浸润调节免疫的机制，为CRC特异性讨论提供丰富素材。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0209\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Abstract 4611: Microbiome-derived indole metabolites and response to immune checkpoint inhibitors in patients with hepatocellular carcinoma\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"CH02\",\n        \"CH03\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"在不可切除HCC患者中，发现血清吲哚丙酸（IPA）水平与ICI持久反应正相关，并关联了Pasteurellaceae和Lachnospiraceae科。研究提出了色氨酸 - 吲哚通路介导免疫调节的假设。该材料提供了特定代谢物作为HCC疗效预测标志物的初步证据，并丰富了代谢机制的多样性。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0210\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Early Prediction of Anti-PD-1 Therapy Response in Hepatocellular Carcinoma Using Gut Microbiota Biomarkers\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"CH02\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该研究利用低丰度微生物特征和神经网络模型，在HCC患者中构建了预测抗PD-1响应的生物标志物（AUROC 0.784）。它展示了从看似无显著关联的数据中提取预测信号的方法论，提示稀有菌种可能在介导疗效中起重要作用，为生物标志物开发提供技术参考案例。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0211\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Helicobacter pylori serology is associated with worse overall survival in patients with melanoma treated with immune checkpoint inhibitors\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"CH01\",\n        \"CH03\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该研究发现H. pylori血清阳性与黑色素瘤及NSCLC患者ICI治疗后OS缩短显著相关，且独立于抗生素暴露和粪便微生物组多样性。这提示上消化道病原体可能通过系统性免疫调节（如改变DC功能）而非肠道菌群重塑来负面影响疗效，拓展了微生物影响ICI的非肠道途径视角。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0212\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Microbiota boost immunotherapy? A meta-analysis dives into fecal microbiota transplantation and immune checkpoint inhibitors\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"CH01\",\n        \"CH04\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该荟萃分析汇总了FMT联合ICI在实体瘤中的临床数据，显示ORR为43%，双药联合时提升至60%。它提出了增加有益菌、提高多样性及调节TME等潜在机制假说，并指出了供体来源和给药途径的异质性。为评估FMT临床有效性和转化瓶颈提供了量化证据和理论框架。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0213\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Antibiotic-Related Changes in Microbiome: The Hidden Villain behind Colorectal Carcinoma Immunotherapy Failure\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"CH01\",\n        \"CH03\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该综述汇总了多项队列和荟萃分析证据，证实抗生素使用与实体瘤（包括CRC）ICI疗效降低（PFS/OS缩短）相关。它详细描述了有益菌增强DC功能和CD8+ T细胞募集、而菌群失调促进Treg扩增的机制。为抗生素作为负面调节因子的临床证据和免疫学机制提供了全面总结。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0214\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"The role of the gut microbiome in immune modulation: implications for autoimmune diseases and cancer therapy\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"CH02\",\n        \"CH03\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该综述列举了Akkermansia, Faecalibacterium等与ICI疗效正相关的物种，并描述了其通过增强DC活性、促进T细胞浸润及SCFAs表观遗传修饰发挥作用的机制。它还提及CAR-T疗法中微生物的影响，可作为平行证据支持微生物调节全身免疫状态从而影响多种免疫治疗结局的观点。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0215\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Microbiome Modulation for the Treatment of Solid Neoplasms\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"CH01\",\n        \"CH04\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该综述总结了特定肠道微生物（Ruminococcaceae, Akkermansia）与ICI改善结局的关联，以及抗生素破坏菌群导致生存率下降的证据。它提供了FMT和益生菌试验的ORR/PFS数据，并讨论了饮食纤维增强后生元产生的机制。为微生物干预的临床现状和方法学挑战提供了概览。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0216\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Perspective on the Role of Gut Microbiome in the Treatment of Hepatocellular Carcinoma with Immune Checkpoint Inhibitors\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"CH02\",\n        \"CH03\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"针对HCC，该综述提供了预测ICI响应的微生物指纹图谱（如响应者富集Akkermansia, Lactobacillus）。它阐述了“肠 - 肝轴”机制，包括菌群失调导致LPS易位引发慢性炎症、次级胆汁酸通过mTOR促进肿瘤发生等路径。为HCC特异性微生物标志物和机制提供了详细背景。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0217\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Myokine-mediated mechanisms of immune checkpoint inhibitors-associated colorectal injury and repair in rectal cancer\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"CH03\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该综述描述了肠道菌群失调导致LPS易位并激活TLR4/NF-κB通路，从而加剧ICI引起的全身和局部炎症。它引入了“肠道 - 肌肉”轴，阐述肌动蛋白（如IL-6, Irisin）如何调节免疫细胞功能和肠道屏障。虽聚焦毒性，但为理解菌群失调放大免疫反应的机制提供了新视角。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0218\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Commensal Bifidobacterium Strains Enhance the Efficacy of Neo-Epitope Based Cancer Vaccines\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"CH03\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"在小鼠模型中，该研究发现双歧杆菌通过维持Muribaculaceae水平和可能的“分子模拟”机制，增强基于新表位癌症疫苗的疗效。虽非ICI研究，但其揭示的微生物通过维持菌群稳态和抗原交叉反应增强免疫治疗的机制，可为理解微生物调节适应性免疫提供类比参考。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0219\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Peripheral blood CD3+HLADR+ cells and associated gut microbiome species predict response and overall survival to immune checkpoint blockade\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"CH02\",\n        \"CH03\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该研究发现外周血活化T细胞（CD3+HLA-DR+）频率与特定肠道微生物（Burkholderiales, B. vulgatus）丰度相关，且联合评分能更好预测OS。提出微生物可能通过调节T细胞活化水平来介导疗效的假设。为“免疫 - 微生物”联合生物标志物及微生物调节全身免疫稳态提供了实证。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0220\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"A Review of Gut Microbiota‐Derived Metabolites in Tumor Progression and Cancer Therapy\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"CH03\",\n        \"CH04\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该综述详细列举了SCFAs、肌苷、MDP等促进ICI疗效的代谢物及其作用路径（如HDAC抑制、A2AR signaling），同时也提到了SCFAs在某些情境下的反面证据。它提供了从受体结合到基因表达调控的多层次机制解释，并讨论了FMT等克服耐药的策略，为代谢物机制提供全面素材。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0221\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Exploring the Frequency and Risk Factors of Hyperprogressive Disease in Patients with Advanced Melanoma Treated with Immune Checkpoint Inhibitors\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"CH01\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该研究报道了黑色素瘤患者ICI治疗后超进展（HPD）的发生率（15.2%）及临床风险因素（如低嗜酸性粒细胞计数）。虽未涉及微生物组，但其揭示了宿主免疫状态与异常疗效模式的关联，可作为讨论ICI疗效异质性和识别高风险人群的背景，提示需探索微生物组在其中的潜在角色。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0222\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"The intratumoral microbiota: a new horizon in cancer immunology\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"CH02\",\n        \"CH03\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该综述聚焦瘤内微生物群（ITM），指出特定微生物丰度与黑色素瘤、胃癌等患者ICI响应及生存期相关。它阐述了ITM通过PRRs激活炎症通路、代谢物表观遗传调控及诱导三级淋巴结构等机制。为理解肿瘤局部微环境中微生物的直接免疫调节作用提供了重要背景和机制框架。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0223\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Association of SCFA in gut microbiome and clinical response in solid cancer patients treated with andi-PD-1 antibody\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"CH02\",\n        \"CH03\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该研究发现实体瘤患者粪便SCFA水平与抗PD-1治疗响应率正相关，响应者fSCFA显著高于非响应者。虽未深入分子机制，但确立了SCFA作为中介变量的可能性，提示微生物代谢活动是连接菌群与宿主免疫反应的关键环节。为代谢物介导效应提供了直接的临床关联证据。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0224\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"From Alpha Diversity to Zeitgebers: Functional Implications and Potential Mechanisms Linking the Gut Microbiome to Sleep and Circadian Disruption (Part II)\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"CH03\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"虽未直接涉及ICI，但该综述详细描述了睡眠/昼夜节律紊乱通过HPA轴、TLR4/LPS信号及胆汁酸受体改变肠道环境和全身免疫状态。这些机制（如SCFAs减少、炎症增加）可能间接影响抗肿瘤免疫，为理解宿主生活方式因素如何通过微生物组调节免疫治疗背景提供了理论框架。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0225\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Investigating Chronic Toxicity, Diet, Patient-Reported Outcomes and the Microbiome in Immunotherapy-Treated Metastatic Melanoma Survivors: A New Frontier\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"CH01\",\n        \"CH05\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该横断面研究发现黑色素瘤幸存者中慢性毒性状态与特定微生物组结构（如F/B比值升高）相关，且添加糖摄入与症状严重程度正相关。它提示微生物组可能作为长期毒性生物标志物，并提出了“饮食 - 微生物组 - 心理”轴线。为讨论ICI长期预后及生活方式干预提供实证线索。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0226\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Combined immune checkpoint inhibitors and ablative radiotherapy in metastatic cancers: a meta-analysis of prospective clinical trials\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"CH01\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该荟萃分析提供了ICI联合放疗在转移性实体瘤中的pooled生存率和毒性数据，指出高剂量和双靶点与更好OS相关但毒性更高。虽未涉及微生物组，但其量化了标准联合治疗的临床基线和风险收益比，可作为评估微生物干预是否能提供“更温和但有效”替代方案的对比参照。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0227\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Abstract 6469: Longitudinal loss of microbiome stability is associated with poor response to immune checkpoint inhibitors in lung cancer and melanoma\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"CH01\",\n        \"CH02\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该研究发现肠道微生物组稳定性丧失（而非静态组成）与NSCLC和黑色素瘤患者ICI疗效差相关。它强调了纵向动态特征作为耐药性预测因子的价值，并开发了基于机器学习的预测指数。为理解微生物群落结构波动性对治疗结局的影响提供了新颖的实证视角和方法论参考。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0228\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"The Gut Microbiome and Epigenomic Reprogramming: Mechanisms, Interactions, and Implications for Human Health and Disease\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"CH03\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该综述详细描述了微生物代谢物（丁酸、PSA、次级胆汁酸）通过抑制HDAC、诱导DNA去甲基化等表观遗传机制调节免疫细胞（特别是Tregs）功能。虽未直接涉及ICI，但这些机制是微生物组调节抗肿瘤免疫的基础生物学原理之一，为解释微生物如何通过表观遗传重塑免疫微环境提供理论支持。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0229\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"The role of gut microbiota in cancer treatment: friend or foe?\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"CH02\",\n        \"CH03\",\n        \"CH04\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该综述列举了与ICI疗效正负相关的特定细菌物种，并详细描述了Bacteroides诱导Th1反应、Akkermansia通过IL-12募集T细胞等机制。它还讨论了FMT、益生菌等调控策略的现状与挑战。为微生物标志物列表、机制解释及临床转化讨论提供了全面且经典的背景素材。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0230\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"283 Safety and efficacy signals in the complete phase I study of live biotherapeutic MRx0518 in combination with pembrolizumab in patients refractory to immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs)\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"CH03\",\n        \"CH04\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该I期研究显示，活体生物疗法MRx0518联合帕博利珠单抗在ICI难治性实体瘤中实现了42%的疾病控制率。机制上，MRx0518通过激活肿瘤TLR5诱导NFκB和T细胞浸润。这为单一菌株疗法通过先天免疫受体激活适应性免疫从而克服ICI耐药提供了初步临床证据和具体机制线索。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0231\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Potential role of gut microbes in the efficacy and toxicity of immune checkpoints inhibitors\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"CH02\",\n        \"CH03\",\n        \"CH04\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该综述提供了不同实体瘤中与ICI疗效及irAEs相关的微生物门类及菌种详细列表，并概述了SCFAs、肌苷等代谢物调节免疫的潜在机制。它还总结了FMT、益生菌等干预手段的临床进展和局限性。为跨癌种比较微生物标志物、机制探讨及干预策略评估提供了综合性素材。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0232\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Multidimensional analysis of the impact of Gemmatimonas, Rhodothermus, and Sutterella on drug and treatment response in colorectal cancer\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"CH02\",\n        \"CH03\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该研究基于TCGA数据，发现特定菌群组合（Gemmatimonas, Sutterella）定义的结直肠癌亚型与免疫治疗反应预测指标（T-cell-inflamed GEP, TIDE）相关。C1亚型具有高T细胞炎症特征，暗示对ICI更敏感。为微生物组通过塑造肿瘤免疫微环境（如巨噬细胞浸润）影响疗效提供了计算预测证据。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0233\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Association of intra-tumoral microbiome and response to immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs) in patients with metastatic renal cell carcinoma (mRCC).\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"CH02\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该小样本研究发现mRCC患者肿瘤内嗜麦芽窄食单胞菌和棒状杆菌丰度与ICI响应正相关。它提示肿瘤局部微生物构成可能独立于肠道菌群调节免疫治疗反应，并为特定癌种（mRCC）提供了肿瘤内微生物作为生物标志物的初步观察性证据，丰富了微生物作用的空间维度。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0234\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Biomarkers of immune checkpoint inhibitor efficacy in cancer.\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"CH01\",\n        \"CH03\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该综述提供了人类队列证据，显示抗生素使用缩短实体瘤患者ICI治疗的PFS/OS，而响应者粪便中Akkermansia muciniphila丰度更高。无菌小鼠FMT实验证实了微生物组的因果作用。为微生物组影响ICI疗效的临床观察和动物实验因果验证提供了关键的基础性证据。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0235\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"T cell receptor therapy against melanoma—Immunotherapy for the future?\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"CH02\",\n        \"CH03\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"虽聚焦TCR疗法，但该综述总结了黑色素瘤ICI治疗中responders富集Ruminococcaceae, Faecalibacterium等菌属的观察数据，并提出有利微生物组通过增强抗原呈递和效应T细胞功能促进疗效的机制。可作为背景材料，说明微生物组调节T细胞功能的普遍性及其在克服TME抑制中的潜在作用。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0236\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Systemic antibiotic exposure and outcomes of immune checkpoint inhibitors in non–small cell lung cancer.\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"CH01\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该大规模荟萃分析（>5万患者）证实全身性抗生素暴露与NSCLC患者ICI治疗后较差的OS和PFS显著相关（HR 1.16）。它为“微生物群介导的疗效受损”假说提供了强有力的流行病学支持，量化了抗生素干扰的临床后果，并强调了优化抗生素管理在ICI治疗中的紧迫性。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0237\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Dietary Amino Acids and the Gut-Microbiome-Immune Axis: Physiological Metabolism and Therapeutic Prospects.\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"CH03\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该综述阐述了氨基酸代谢产物作为微生物 - 宿主通讯介质的机制，包括通过TLRs、AhR等受体调节免疫稳态。虽未直接涉及ICI，但这些基础生理机制解释了肠道微生物如何通过代谢活动系统性影响宿主免疫状态，为理解微生物调节抗肿瘤免疫的潜在生化路径提供了理论背景。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0238\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"Delineating the role of the microbiome and tumor microenvironment interactions driving mucosal melanoma (MM) response and resistance to immune checkpoint inhibitor (ICI) treatment.\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"CH02\",\n        \"CH03\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"针对罕见的黏膜黑色素瘤，该研究发现响应者肠道富集Streptococcus, Collinsella等菌，且肿瘤微环境中CD56/CD20高表达。它揭示了不同原发部位（鼻口腔vs皮肤）的微生物异质性及其与免疫特征的关联，为理解解剖部位特异性微生物 - 免疫互作提供了独特案例。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0239\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"De-correlating immune checkpoint inhibitor toxicity and response in melanoma via the microbiome.\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"CH02\",\n        \"CH03\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该研究发现特定菌群（Bacteroides, Blautia）与ICI响应正相关，而Prevotella与无响应相关。重要的是，它识别出Eubacterium siraeum与无irAE的响应相关，提示微生物组特征可能“解耦”疗效与毒性。为通过微生物组特征实现个性化治疗（平衡疗效与安全性）提供了实证线索。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0240\",\n      \"paper_title\": \"From obesity to cancer: Gut microbiome mechanisms, biomarkers, and U.S. public health strategies\",\n      \"chapter_ids\": [\n        \"CH03\"\n      ],\n      \"specific_usable_material\": \"该综述描述了微生物组失调通过TLR/NF-κB通路和细胞因子网络（IL-6, TNF-α）维持慢性低度炎症和免疫抑制微环境的机制。虽聚焦肥胖和CRC自然病程，但这些基础免疫调节机制有助于解释为何某些促炎微生物特征可能与较差的免疫治疗预后相关，提供背景性机制解释。\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
        "reasoning_content": "The user wants me to route each source in the candidate batch to the appropriate chapters in the shared outline. I need to:\n\n1. Read each source's B planning card carefully\n2. Check the actual research type, object, conditions, material depth\n3. Route to appropriate chapter(s) based on what the source actually contributes\n4. Write specific_usable_material in Chinese (80-150 characters) indicating concrete usable facts or comparison angles\n5. Not force irrelevant sources into chapters\n6. Return JSON with source_routes array\n\nLet me analyze each source:\n\nP0181: About enterotype from older individuals enabling favorable ICB responses. Has clinical meta-analysis evidence for elderly patients + mouse FMT validation. Relevant to CH01 (clinical evidence), CH02 (microbial features), CH03 (mechanisms - T cell remodeling).\n\nP0182: Gut microbiome associates with ICI outcomes in NSCLC (Japanese cohort). 16S sequencing, observational. Specific taxa (Ruminococcaceae UCG 13, Agathobacter) associated with better outcomes. Antibiotic use reduces beneficial taxa. Relevant to CH01, CH02, CH03.\n\nP0183: Full review on gut-lung-immune axis in NSCLC. Comprehensive mechanism background. Relevant to CH02, CH03, CH05 (limitations).\n\nP0184: TIL therapy review from SITC. Only briefly mentions microbiome in general terms. Not directly about ICI-microbiome interaction. Should be minimally used or noted as limited relevance. Could go to CH05 as background context.\n\nP0185: PPI use impact on ICI efficacy across cancer types. Observational, no microbiome data directly. Clinical association that needs mechanistic explanation. Relevant to CH01 (clinical evidence of drug interactions), CH05 (limitations - no mechanism).\n\nP0186: Comparative genomics of Lachnospiraceae strains. Mouse model + genomic analysis. \n\nP0187: 2018 review on prognostic factors for CPI. Has section on gut microbiota with specific species. Good for CH02, CH03 background.\n\nP0188: Intestinal fungal signatures meta-analysis. Multi-cohort. Specific fungal species associated with ICI efficacy in melanoma vs NSCLC. Mouse experiments for D. hansenii. Relevant to CH02 (fungal features), CH03 (mechanisms).\n\nP0189: ADC + ICI synergy review. Not directly about microbiome. Only briefly mentions microbiome as future direction. Limited relevance - could go to CH05 as context.\n\nP0190: OMVs from gut microbiome eliciting cross-reactive T cells. Mouse model, molecular mimicry mechanism. Relevant to CH03 (mechanisms).\n\nP0191: RCC ICI review with microbiome section. Lists specific bacteria, mentions FMT/probiotics. Relevant to CH02, CH03, CH04.\n\nP0192: Full review on gut microbiota influence on immunotherapy. Comprehensive mechanisms, clinical strategies. Relevant to CH02, CH03, CH04, CH05.\n\nP0193: Veillonella and Streptococcus associated with aging and ICI efficacy in solid tumors. Small cohort, observational. Relevant to CH01, CH02, CH03.\n\nP0194: Microbiome-driven diagnostic and therapeutic strategies review. Covers specific bacteria, mechanisms, FMT. Relevant to CH02, CH03, CH04.\n\nP0195: DAT metabolite enhances T-cell priming and ICI. Mouse model, IFN-I pathway. Relevant to CH03 (mechanisms), CH04 (metabolite intervention).\n\nP0196: Immunometabolism and microbiota crosstalk review. Comprehensive mechanisms including SCFAs, tryptophan, bile acids. Relevant to CH03, CH05.\n\nP0197: FMT-LUMINate trial abstract. FMT + ICI in lung cancer and melanoma. Clinical ORR data, toxicity differences, P. copri association with irAE. Relevant to CH01, CH03, CH04.\n\nP0198: Fasting mediated microbiome modulation in RCC. Abstract only. TRE + ICI, FMT validation, tryptophan metabolites. Relevant to CH01, CH03, CH04.\n\nP0199: Baseline gut microbiota in HNC radiotherapy (not ICI). Limited relevance - different treatment modality. Could note in CH05 as methodological reference.\n\nP0200: Integrative stratification using host and microbial signatures in NSCLC. Longitudinal dynamics, microbial score. Relevant to CH01, CH02.\n\nP0201: Natural polyphenol (castalagin) circumvents anti-PD-1 resistance via microbiota. Mouse model + patient FMT. Ruminococcus enrichment, bile acid metabolism. Relevant to CH03, CH04.\n\nP0202: Biomarkers in melanoma review. Has microbiome section with specific taxa, antibiotic impact. Relevant to CH02, CH03.\n\nP0203: Gut microbiome in autoimmune disease treatment. Mainly uses tumor/ICI data as evidence. Limited direct relevance - could use for CH03 mechanism background with caution.\n\nP0204: Multi-kingdom gut microbiota in HCC ICI. Bacteria + fungi + metabolites. Predictive model. Relevant to CH01, CH02.\n\nP0205: EGFR-mutated NSCLC microbiota and ICI. Specific markers differ from EGFR-wild type. Antibiotic impact, metabolites. Relevant to CH01, CH02, CH03.\n\nP0206: Microbiome and genitourinary tumors review (2019). A. muciniphila mechanism, antibiotic impact. Relevant to CH02, CH03.\n\nP0207: ASD microbiome review. Not cancer/ICI. Very limited relevance - only general immune modulation background. Should be noted as not directly relevant.\n\nP0208: CRC microbiome alterations review. Detailed mechanisms, MSI vs MSS differences, intervention strategies. Relevant to CH02, CH03, CH04, CH05.\n\nP0209: Indole metabolites and ICI in HCC abstract. IPA association, Pasteurellaceae/Lachnospiraceae. Relevant to CH02, CH03.\n\nP0210: Early prediction of anti-PD-1 response in HCC using microbiota. Neural network model, 8 taxa. Relevant to CH01, CH02.\n\nP0211: H. pylori serology associated with worse OS in melanoma/NSCLC ICI. Independent of fecal microbiome. Relevant to CH01, CH03 (non-gut microbiome effects).\n\nP0212: FMT + ICI meta-analysis. ORR 43%, double checkpoint better. Mechanism hypotheses. Relevant to CH01, CH03, CH04.\n\nP0213: Antibiotic-related microbiome changes in CRC immunotherapy review. Specific bacterial markers, mechanisms. Relevant to CH01, CH02, CH03.\n\nP0214: Gut microbiome in immune modulation review (autoimmune + cancer). Specific bacteria, mechanisms, CAR-T comparison. Relevant to CH02, CH03.\n\nP0215: Microbiome modulation for solid neoplasms review (JCO 2025). Clinical trial landscape, specific markers, challenges. Relevant to CH01, CH02, CH04, CH05.\n\nP0216: HCC microbiome perspective review. Specific taxa for HCC, gut-liver axis mechanisms. Relevant to CH02, CH03, CH04.\n\nP0217: Myokine-mediated ICI colorectal injury review. Microbiome dysbiosis → LPS → TLR4/NF-κB. Relevant to CH03 (mechanisms), CH05.\n\nP0218: Bifidobacterium enhances cancer vaccine efficacy (not ICI). Mouse model, molecular mimicry. Limited relevance - different immunotherapy type. Could use for CH03 mechanism comparison.\n\nP0219: Peripheral blood CD3+HLADR+ and gut microbiome predict ICI response. Combined score. Relevant to CH01, CH02, CH03.\n\nP0220: Microbiota-derived metabolites review. SCFAs, inosine, MDP, TMAO mechanisms. Relevant to CH02, CH03.\n\nP0221: Hyperprogressive disease in melanoma ICI. Clinical risk factors, eosinophils. No microbiome data. Limited relevance - CH05 only as clinical context.\n\nP0222: Intratumoral microbiota review. Mechanisms, biomarkers, intervention strategies. Relevant to CH02, CH03, CH04.\n\nP0223: SCFA and anti-PD-1 response abstract. Clinical correlation. Relevant to CH01, CH02, CH",
